Support the front so the wheel is off the ground and both forks are fully extended. Briefly open each fork air-release screw/plug bolt to vent built-up air, then close it; do this after practice and between motos. Honda’s guided job is **“Release built-up air from the fork”**—tap **“Working on the bike?”** above the message box to walk through it.
Bleed the forks with them fully extended and the front wheel off the ground—after practice and between motos.
