Yes. Give it a short, easy first ride and cycle the suspension over ordinary bumps before pushing the pace; fresh seals and components can feel tight at first. There’s no confirmed break-in lap count here, so follow the rebuilder’s instructions if they gave you one. After riding, with the fork fully extended and the front wheel off the ground, release built-up air from the fork plugs. Stop if you find an oil leak.
Yes—give new or freshly rebuilt suspension an easy first ride before judging the setup. Recheck for leaks and release fork air afterward.
